<p>Lebanese officials and media groups accused Israel of committing a war crime after an Israeli strike in south Lebanon killed journalist Amal Khalil, prompting public mourning and official condemnation. Reports said Khalil died in the strike, and some accounts said she had taken shelter before the building where she was located was hit; rescuers said they could not reach the rubble before her body was recovered. Her killing has sharpened scrutiny of the dangers journalists face while covering the Israel-Lebanon conflict and renewed debate over whether reporters and rescue workers are being unlawfully targeted during military operations. Funeral ceremonies in Lebanon drew mourners honoring Khalil’s reporting, underscoring broader concern about press freedom in a cross-border conflict that has repeatedly struck southern Lebanese communities.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/mYyNSJ51THtj9XvKM0KVFgPOKFk-Q3PwfcdBscYyxf_ZSS4CMfE6Knxo_6U0AgyypEBc7tE5DZqtk0dzg5dBhtWREqYbCGuhK_j-rbWqzlvNi9Q9cxPJDaBXVvwSZduJ4-oPBWtL4HLxvUSOCjfzv_9ZrRGvIYlVjLmBph3E7uC2bk9ywPnI6gTZpFCjxUpHoHpKtvdYaL3XIXLXzbnt5OFdj_RUT6rnsBgEpxcfO-YdyUE7fDrBfA7RlQnSEaNGg2TCVh9FBmwsP9Bm' alt='Family members of Amal Khalil at her funeral in Baysariyeh, Lebanon, on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Union allegation: A journalists&#x27; union said rescuers were blocked from reaching the destroyed building where Khalil remained trapped, adding a second layer of controversy beyond the strike itself.</li><li>CPJ response: The Committee to Protect Journalists called Khalil’s killing a &quot;grave breach of international humanitarian law,&quot; according to Nova Media’s reporting.</li><li>Official language: Lebanese leaders publicly called the strike &quot;war crimes,&quot; signaling that they want the killing treated as more than a battlefield casualty.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Lebanese government: Lebanese leaders condemned the strike as a war crime and cast Khalil’s killing as an attack that demands international accountability. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1994569/lebanese-leaders-condemn-war-crimes-after-israeli-strike-kills-journalist'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Committee to Protect Journalists: The press freedom group described the killing as a grave breach of international humanitarian law, reflecting deep concern about protections for reporters in conflict zones. (<a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/04/23/israel-kills-top-journalist-then-attacks-rescuers-trying-to-save-her/'>Novara Media</a>)</li><li>Rescue workers and journalists&#x27; union: Their account said emergency crews could not promptly reach the rubble, shifting attention to the treatment of rescuers as well as the original strike. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/lebanon-israel-war-crime-journalist-killed-drone-strike/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Mourners and colleagues: Funeral attendance and tributes highlighted Khalil’s reputation for courageous field reporting. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/23/world/middleeast/lebanese-journalist-amal-khalil-killed-israeli-strike.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/lebanon-israel-war-crime-journalist-killed-drone-strike/'>Lebanon accuses Israel of war crime in killing of journalist</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/04/23/israel-kills-top-journalist-then-attacks-rescuers-trying-to-save-her/'>Israel Kills Top Journalist Then Attacks Rescuers Trying to Save Her</a> - novaramedia.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/23/world/middleeast/lebanese-journalist-amal-khalil-killed-israeli-strike.html'>Lebanese Journalist Killed in Israeli Strike Was Known for Being Intrepid</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1994569/lebanese-leaders-condemn-war-crimes-after-israeli-strike-kills-journalist'>Lebanese leaders condemn ‘war crimes’ after Israeli strike kills journalist</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https: